Prospero's Hoard bundles third-party material. Each item keeps its own license and attribution.

Sound-effects engine (prosperos_hoard/editing/foley/)
  Procedural sound-effect bank, kit presets and take-measurement code, vendored and adapted
  (own module names, a numpy-only WAV reader/writer, no dependency on the original repository).
  Source: Earshot v0.4.0, commit 591fa3e028032e6dce56620a20e932e35667e8d8, by Leon Lin.
  License: MIT. The original license text is kept in prosperos_hoard/editing/foley/LICENSE.earshot
  and the details of what changed in prosperos_hoard/editing/foley/NOTICE.

Direction style cards (prosperos_hoard/style_library/)
  Seventy-four written film styles used as style cards: sections (essence, materials, colour, type, motion,
  camera, sound, native moves, pitfalls) and the prompts of a second collection, kept as text and split by the
  parsers in prosperos_hoard/style_cards.py. Every card carries its licence, attribution and source link.
  Source 1: Lemo-Opuscar by LemoLab, commit 413a6bd6d78ebd3bdd5abaec9538a26867f890df, 59 styles.
    https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar
    License: MIT for the code and the style texts (LICENSE.lemo-opuscar). The demo films and stills of that
    project are CC BY 4.0 and are NOT included here.
  Source 2: MG Styles 15 by Vincentwei1021, commit 49052d80bfaf9fa8412cc9710530e5e95a3b8d8c, 15 prompts.
    https://github.com/Vincentwei1021/mg-styles-15
    License: MIT for the code, prompts and docs (LICENSE.mg-styles-15). Its films and third-party files keep
    their own licences and are NOT included here.
  A variant made from a card keeps the licence, the attribution and the link of the card it comes from.

Methods followed (no code copied):
  Edit plans (plan with input fingerprints, run, verify against platform specs, contact sheet): the workflow of
    kajisho5/ffmpeg-skill, MIT. https://github.com/kajisho5/ffmpeg-skill
  Workflow preflight (node classes against /object_info, model files against the loader lists): the pattern of
    D3voz/openjutsu, MIT. https://github.com/D3voz/openjutsu
  Treatment-first productions (logline, three structures and the pick, benchmark, shot list with reasons, cue map):
    the DIRECTOR.md method of lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT. https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar
  Anti-slideshow lint for HTML motion (three or more opacity-only sections are rejected): the rule of
    bangtutorial/bang-motion, MIT. https://github.com/bangtutorial/bang-motion

Director catalog (prosperos_hoard/director.py)
  The 28 motion presets (camera, epic camera, effects, mood), the direction axes (genre with the axes it sets,
  lens, framing, light, film stock, look, grade), the decade looks from 1960 to 2020 and the forgiving reading of a
  model's shot list are adapted from OpenField by David Wexler / Strangeloop Studios, commit
  1c364121cd299da3959d7c8e77e12e9295a37943. https://github.com/wexloops/openfield
  License: MIT, text kept in prosperos_hoard/LICENSE.openfield. Prompt texts kept; names, Spanish labels,
  formats and the production pipeline are this studio's own.
